      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[7]_{11}?$\n\n- $18$\n- $-4$\n- $15$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue class $[7]_{11}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $7$ modulo $11.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[7]_{11} & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡7\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)} \\\\  & ={x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=7+11k,\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={7+11k\\,|\\,k\\in Z} \\\\  & ={…,\\,7-2\\cdot 11,\\,7-11,\\,7,\\,7+11,\\,7+2\\cdot 11,…} \\\\  & ={…,-15,-4,7,18,29,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-4$ and $18$ belong to $[7]_{11},$ while $15$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
